        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 12,
        "titulo": "Where to? «в» and «на» + accusative",
        "explicacao": "We have already seen «Где?» (where): «в» + prepositional («в магазине»). To ask «Куда?» (where to, with movement), use the ACCUSATIVE: «Я иду в магазин», «Я еду на работу». In short: standing still → prepositional; moving → accusative. For \"home\" there is a word of its own, with no preposition: «домой» (going home); \"at home\" is «дома». The verbs «идти» (on foot) and «ехать» (by bus, car or train) are irregular: learn the forms.",
        "comparacao": "in English we say \"in the shop\" for place and \"to the shop\" for movement. Russian keeps the same preposition and changes the ending of the word.",
